## Fixed and frozen mirror constraint

A descriptor fix cannot report configurable:false while its target mirror remains configurable. Nor can a get trap return a fresh child wrapper for a frozen nonwritable data property whose target stores a different object: Proxy invariants prohibit both. A possible bounded form resolves and guards a descriptor's value at the actual descriptor request, materializes that guarded value with the original flags in the mirror and memoizes it for subsequent reads. Unknown values stop before materialization. That is a design constraint, not implemented code. Construction must not eagerly read an unknown property simply to populate its mirror.

